\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab Not for our sins alone
\par \pard\li720 Thy mercy, Lord, we sue ;
\par Let fall Thy pitying glance
\par On our devotions too -
\par What we have done for Thee,
\par And what we think to do.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab The holiest hours we spend
\par \pard\li720 In prayer upon our knees,
\par The times when most we deem
\par Our songs of praise will please,
\par Thou searcher of all hearts,
\par Forgiveness pour on these.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab And all the gifts we bring,
\par \pard\li720 And all the vows we make,
\par And all the acts of love
\par We plan for Thy dear sake,
\par Into thy pardoning thought,
\par O God of mercy, take.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab And most when we, Thy flock,
\par \pard\li720 Before thine altar bend,
\par And strange bewildering thoughts
\par With those sweet moments blend,
\par By Him whose death we plead,
\par Good Lord, thy help extend.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.\tab Bow down Thine ear and hear :
\par \pard\li720 Open Thine eyes and see :
\par Our very love is shame ;
\par And we must come to Thee
\par To make it, of Thy grace,
\par What Thou wouldst have it be.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

